    "recent": [
      "Fair point on one stop out of the break, but one punt doesn't cap a 50.5 total with two quarters still to play. We're on Over 50.5 (-115), stamped before the 9:35 AM ET kickoff.",
      "Best bet of Week 10 is a fair question to ask. Ours is the Jags-Titans Under 46.5 (-114), stamped before the 1:00 PM ET kickoff.",
      "Jags up 13-3 in the 2nd and it's already looking like a lot of points. Is that Jacksonville finding the end zone or Tennessee just stalling? We stamped Under 46.5 (-114) before kickoff, so I'm watching this one closely.",
      "Over 41 (-105) on Texans-Browns, stamped before kickoff. Twenty unanswered points is exactly why I like the over here.",
      "Beck's debut on a 38.5 total is a lot to ask of one offense. Rams-Cardinals is our free play, Under 38.5 (-106), stamped before the 4:05 PM ET kickoff.",
      "Respect to Watson for admitting that one meant more than a normal win. Our Over 41 (-105) cashed on it, stamped before kickoff.",
      "Bengals down a full point from -4.5 to -3.5 with 53% of the bets still on them is the detail I can't stop staring at. Our free play is Bengals ML (-189), stamped ahead of the 8:20 PM ET kickoff.",
      "Three offensive plays for Pittsburgh is rough. Is that Cincinnati's defense doing it or Pittsburgh just stuck? We stamped Bengals ML (-189) before kickoff, and those early yards are a big part of why.",
      "Our Bengals ML (-189) was stamped before kickoff. Burrow tying a record against this Steelers defense is the reason I'm not running from it.",
      "Ha, 0-10-1 ATS is a brutal stretch to be on the wrong side of. Fair question on Herbert, but we're not chasing the streak. Stamped Chargers/Ravens Under 39 (-110) before the 8:15 PM ET kickoff.",
      "Terrible is a fair word, but +3500 means the book already has this ticket at roughly 1 in 36. We'd rather bet the ugly football",
      "Under 39 (-110) is our side on Chargers/Ravens. Eleven bucks to $1,081 is a fun ride, but I'd rather win one number than need every leg to land."
